{# THE PATROLS MONTH, drawn ONCE for both of the places it appears — the
   dashboard's calendar widget and the calendar tab.

   THE MONTH IS THE ATLAS'S AND NOT THIS MODULE'S. The grid, the day head, the
   cell, its fixed height, the day number, the day's count, the mark, the
   "+N more" and the stepper all come out of `atlas_calendar()`; this module
   ships no month grid of its own and says only what happened on which day
   (Uhifadhi\Patrol\Service\PatrolCalendar). That is the whole bargain of the
   component, and the reason a busy week cannot make the month taller than a
   quiet one.

   THE CARD IS THIS MODULE'S. The `.c` shell, its tab and the month in the
   caption are the dashboard card every widget wears; everything inside the
   card below the caption is the component's.

   THE FEED IS HANDED OVER BY THE CONTROLLER rather than reached for as a
   global: a template that resolved a service would be a template with a
   container in it.

   Bindings:
     area        the area on screen, for nothing but the card's own links
     feed        the CalendarFeedInterface this month is asked of
     scope       what to narrow it to — PatrolCalendar::scopeFor()
     month       a \DateTimeImmutable inside the month being drawn
     now         the viewer's instant, so the right square is ringed
     previousUrl where ‹ goes, and nextUrl where › goes
     controls    the surface's OWN control, already rendered, drawn at the
                 trailing end of the stepper row; '' where the surface's
                 filter is already on screen somewhere else #}
<div class="c">
    <span class="tab">Patrol calendar<span class="src">&middot; {{ month|date('F Y')|lower }}</span></span>
    {{ atlas_calendar(
        feed,
        month|date('Y-m'),
        scope,
        today: now,
        previousUrl: previousUrl,
        nextUrl: nextUrl,
        controls: controls|default('')
    ) }}
</div>
